I see I have one custom component—the backend—along with clients, but the server is still largely a "dumb relay," storing ciphertext and the device key directory. I think simplifying the document by removing scale targets could help, while still addressing failure scenarios. 

If the backend is down, clients can’t relay messages, but they might keep sending to known device keys. If only the directory API fails, clients can still send using cached sessions. I want to address that if a device is compromised, an admin key’s theft can lead to unauthorized enrollments, so users should mandate manual approval and notifications for added security.
